Subject: visionOS 3D: GE Plus's crosshair gets the reticle's depth too (D-064)

0035 gives the crosshair the depth of whatever it points at by opening a
depth span around the sight types' switch in sightDraw(). GE Plus draws its
own crosshair (gehud.c, GoldenEye's sight for anything of GoldenEye's in the
hand on a converted level) from an early return ABOVE that switch, so in 3D
it never got the span: measured in Dam on the Vision Pro simulator, the
crosshair sat at 0 px disparity in both eyes while the cliff and barriers
behind it were at +23..+29 px - on the panel, in front of what it aimed at.

The span now opens before GE Plus's branch and that branch closes it before
returning. Nothing else moves: in 2D (and on every other platform) the block
is the same runtime-gated / compiled-out no-op it was, so the M-001 display
list is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/game/sight.c b/src/game/sight.c
index 8fc733a07..e10ee72a4 100644
--- a/src/game/sight.c
+++ b/src/game/sight.c
@@ -1848,6 +1848,22 @@ Gfx *sightDraw(Gfx *gdl, bool sighton, s32 sight)
 
 	sightTick(sighton);
 
+#if defined(TARGET_OS_VISION) && TARGET_OS_VISION
+	// D-064: one trace, one tag, and every rectangle of the reticle inside the
+	// span gets it. The tag is a G_NOOP, so on every other platform this is a
+	// dead branch the preprocessor removes entirely — and in 2D on visionOS the
+	// runtime gate makes the display list byte-identical to the one the oracle
+	// walks, which is what the M-001 replay compares. Opened before GE Plus's
+	// own crosshair below, which returns early: it had no depth in 3D (it sat
+	// on the panel in both eyes, in front of whatever it pointed at).
+	const bool stereo3d = pdVisionStereoIsActive() != 0;
+
+	if (stereo3d) {
+		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLTAG_DEPTH((s32)sightReticleDepth(crossx, crossy)));
+		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_BEGIN);
+	}
+#endif
+
 #ifndef PLATFORM_N64
 	// GoldenEye's own crosshair for anything of GoldenEye's in the hand on GE
 	// Plus's levels (gehud.c). The watch's SIGHT ON-SCREEN is Sight on Screen,
@@ -1862,23 +1878,15 @@ Gfx *sightDraw(Gfx *gdl, bool sighton, s32 sight)
 			gdl = geHudRenderSight(gdl, crossx, crossy);
 		}
 
-		g_ScaleX = 1;
-
-		return gdl;
-	}
+#if defined(TARGET_OS_VISION) && TARGET_OS_VISION
+		if (stereo3d) {
+			gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_END);
+		}
 #endif
 
-#if defined(TARGET_OS_VISION) && TARGET_OS_VISION
-	// D-064: one trace, one tag, and every rectangle of the reticle inside the
-	// span gets it. The tag is a G_NOOP, so on every other platform this is a
-	// dead branch the preprocessor removes entirely — and in 2D on visionOS the
-	// runtime gate makes the display list byte-identical to the one the oracle
-	// walks, which is what the M-001 replay compares.
-	const bool stereo3d = pdVisionStereoIsActive() != 0;
+		g_ScaleX = 1;
 
-	if (stereo3d) {
-		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLTAG_DEPTH((s32)sightReticleDepth(crossx, crossy)));
-		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_DEPTH_BEGIN);
+		return gdl;
 	}
 #endif
 
